---
import LayoutPage from "@layouts/LayoutPage.astro";
---

<LayoutPage
  title="About Chris Simmons"
  description="Senior frontend developer and design systems engineer with 25+ years of experience. Creator of Skeleton, an open-source design system and component library for React and Svelte."
>
  <main class="p-4 py-12 md:py-24">
    <div class="container mx-auto">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[48px_auto_1fr] gap-4 md:gap-8">
        <!-- Heading 1 -->
        <h1
          class="h1 md:[writing-mode:vertical-rl] md:rotate-180 md:self-start"
        >
          <span>ABOUT</span>
        </h1>
        <!-- Horz Rule -->
        <div class="hidden md:block">
          <hr class="vr border-dashed" />
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-10">
          <p class="hidden md:block text-4xl font-bold">Hi, I'm Chris 👋</p>
          <section class="space-y-4 text-lg md:text-2xl font-medium">
            <p>
              I'm a senior frontend developer and design systems engineer with
              over 25 years of experience. I build production web platforms,
              design systems, and component libraries, and I care about the
              details that make an interface feel right to the people using it.
              I make time to research, tinker, and learn something new every
              day.
            </p>
          </section>
          <hr class="hr" />
          <!-- About Text -->
          <section class="space-y-4 md:text-xl">
            <h2 class="h2">My Story</h2>
            <p>
              I discovered my passion for programming and design while taking
              classes in Visual Basic and Photoshop in high school. I'm also a
              lifelong fan of video games, which began when I received my first
              console as a kid, a classic Nintendo Entertainment System. I still
              remember the magic of picking up that controller and making Mario
              run and jump across the screen (occasionally to his untimely
              death). That spark set me on the path to design and development.
            </p>
            <p>
              That passion grew into a career spanning photography, newspapers
              and national broadcast media, a digital agency, and a number of
              tech startups. Along the way I created <a
                class="anchor"
                href="https://skeleton.dev/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer">Skeleton</a
              >, a free and open-source design system and component library for
              React and Svelte that now sees over 300k downloads a month. I
              serve as its core maintainer and co-founded <a
                class="anchor"
                href="https://www.skeletonlabs.co/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer">Skeleton Labs</a
              > to support the project. It's been a privilege to work alongside some
              of the most talented people in the industry, building platforms for
              the web, video games, and open source.
            </p>
            <p>
              These days my focus is on design systems, accessibility, and the
              handoff between design and development. I use LLM tools where they
              genuinely help, such as prototyping or importing and structuring
              content, but everything I ship is still reviewed, tested, and
              understood by a human in the loop.
            </p>
          </section>
          <!-- My Superpower -->
          <section class="space-y-4 md:text-xl">
            <h2 class="h2">My Superpower</h2>
            <p>
              I believe my strength lies not just in writing code or designing
              interfaces, but in solving real-world problems. I pride myself on
              my ability to listen, learn, and figure out what a project truly
              needs, then deliver at every step from concept to execution.
              Whether you're building a web application, maturing a design
              system, or growing a team's development process, I'd love to help
              move your project forward.
            </p>
          </section>
          <!-- Personal Life -->
          <section class="space-y-4 md:text-xl">
            <h2 class="h2">Personal Life</h2>
            <p>
              Outside of work, I love to travel, get lost in a good RPG, and
              debate movies with friends late into the night. I'm a
              self-described foodie who enjoys cooking and the occasional craft
              beer. I also share my home with the cutest calico cat in the
              world, <a
                href="https://photos.app.goo.gl/coXpCkLtZuKDumrt7"
                target="_blank"
                class="anchor">Pumpkin</a
              >, who's as rambunctious as she is spoiled.
            </p>
          </section>
          <!-- Contact Me -->
          <section class="space-y-4 md:text-xl">
            <h2 class="h2">Contact Me</h2>
            <p>
              I'm currently available for full-time roles. I'm currently based
              in North Texas and open to remote work or relocating for the right
              team. If you think I'd be a good fit, reach out at
              <a href="mailto:chris@skeleton.dev" class="anchor">
                chris@skeleton.dev</a
              >.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</LayoutPage>
